 - `shipments.create_shipment(customer_id, weight_kg, zone)`: book a shipment
 - `shipments.get_shipment(shipment_id)`: fetch one shipment
+- `shipments.split_shipment(shipment_id, weights) -> list[Shipment]`: replace a "created" shipment with one new shipment per weight (same customer and zone), in the order given; the original gets status "split".
+  - `E_NOT_FOUND`: no shipment with that id.
+  - `E_BAD_INPUT`: `weights` is not a list/tuple of at least two weights.
+  - `E_BAD_WEIGHT`: a weight is not a positive number, or the weights do not add up to the shipment's weight (compared to the gram).
+  - `E_BAD_STATE`: the shipment is not in status "created".
 
